The bearded fellow was definitely lying. Ragnar got angry; within a second he seized the bloke's shoulder and before the poor man was able to figure out what was going on, dragged him into a narrow side street.
"I saw you reading the announcement, tell me what it says and I will let you go. But don't even think of lying! Well?" Ragnar shook the bearded fellow.
"Well, it demands someone go kill a monster," the robust fellow said, stammering, "and the chamberlain will reward whoever can." Ragnar decided that he would likely find more information from the chamberlain himself, and so let the citizen go, to his great relief. Then the Lemurian headed straight to the chamberlain.